      <section class="check-understanding">
        <title>Activity</title>
        <exercise id="_35f8f732-434d-4d07-9274-b87ec33765ee" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>Determine if the vertex corresponds to the maximum or the minimum value of the function \(f(x)=-(x−4)^2+6\).</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! The answer is maximum. The leading coefficient is negative, so the parabola opens down.</para>
            <para>Incorrect. The correct answer is maximum. The leading coefficient is negative, so the parabola opens down.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="_0485fc99-f31c-46b4-8d28-4d62ed99a810" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>Determine if the vertex corresponds to the maximum or the minimum value of the function \(g(x)=(x+7)^2−3\).</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! The answer is minimum. The leading coefficient is positive, so the parabola opens up.</para>
            <para>Incorrect. The correct answer is minimum. The leading coefficient is positive, so the parabola opens up.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="da068d33-ced2-4d24-a7a9-0cab78d1f5bf" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>Determine if the vertex corresponds to the maximum or the minimum value of the function \(h(x)=4(x+5)^2+7\).</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! The answer is minimum. The leading coefficient is positive, so the parabola opens up.</para>
            <para>Incorrect. The correct answer is minimum. The leading coefficient is positive, so the parabola opens up.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="_39283ad7-e025-4abc-bdfe-0f2a4f98d6af" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>Determine if the vertex corresponds to the maximum or the minimum value of the function \(k(x)=x^2−6x−3\).</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! The answer is minimum. The leading coefficient is positive, so the parabola opens up.</para>
            <para>Incorrect. The correct answer is minimum. The leading coefficient is positive, so the parabola opens up.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="_973a07e0-cf6d-4808-8a08-f933319bfa50" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>Determine if the vertex corresponds to the maximum or the minimum value of the function \(m(x)=-x^2+8x\).</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! The answer is maximum. The leading coefficient is negative, so the parabola opens down.</para>
            <para>Incorrect. The correct answer is maximum. The leading coefficient is negative, so the parabola opens down.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
      </section>
